   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.1435719831849336, 'original_motivation': "There is no known direct causal relationship where '24/7-care mentality' causes 'Spatial Scale' or vice versa. Changes in the mentality towards continuous care do not directly cause changes in the spatial scale at which care is provided, nor does spatial scale directly alter care mentality. No clear mechanism exists linking these two variables causally within the system. Therefore, no causal link should be included in the CLD.", 'session_id': 'ceeb15de-be05-4191-92e3-ade330d6381d', 'judge_perplexity': 1.5071287664065647, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.07939129681129106, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "CORRECT", "score": 1.0, "reason": "The explanation logically connects the 24/7-care mentality to an increased spatial scale by arguing that continuous care necessitates oversight of more areas, thus expanding management across a larger geographic scope. The reasoning is internally coherent and follows a plausible causal pathway from the source to the target variable.\\nVERDICT: CORRECT\\nSCORE: 1.0"}], "aggregate_score": 1.0, "aggregate_verdict": "CORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6593101035621329, 'motivation': 'Adopting a 24/7-care mentality directly increases the spatial scale of management practices, as the need for constant monitoring and intervention requires expanding oversight across larger geographic areas. This expanded scale ensures all areas receive continuous care, thus making 24/7-care a driving force behind larger spatial management.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 1.0, 'judge_verdict': 'CORRECT', 'spurious_motivation': 'Adopting a 24/7-care mentality directly increases the spatial scale of management practices, as the need for constant monitoring and intervention requires expanding oversight across larger geographic areas. This expanded scale ensures all areas receive continuous care, thus making 24/7-care a driving force behind larger spatial management.', 'judge_min_prob': 0.052248613006346485, 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.7510010148239676, 'judge_token_prob_slope': 0.0015875501070187694, 'judge_prob_std': 0.2817646124183998}

36. 24/7-care mentality-[POSITIVE]->Acute care demand leading to an ED visit
   Properties: {'session_id': 'ceeb15de-be05-4191-92e3-ade330d6381d', 'judge_perplexity': 4.97770201500709e+34, 'citations': ['https://journalofethics.ama-assn.org/article/nonurgent-care-emergency-department-bane-or-boon/2010-06', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8414690/', 'https://data.cms.gov/provider-data/topics/hospitals/timely-effective-care', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10913567/'], 'judge_prob_variance': 0.09891335252666257, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "CORRECT", "score": 1.0, "reason": "The explanation provides a clear causal chain: a 24/7-care mentality influences institutional protocols and resource allocation, which in turn convey to the public that emergency departments are always available for any healthcare need. This signaling is posited to lead to increased acute care demand and more ED visits. The logic is internally consistent, and the steps are plausibly connected. However, the explanation could be stronger if it clarified why this signaling necessarily increases demand, rather than simply accommodating existing demand. Still, the causal pathway as described is reasonable and avoids logical fallacies.\\nVERDICT: CORRECT\\nSCORE: 1.0"}], "aggregate_score": 1.0, "aggregate_verdict": "CORRECT"}', 'max_prob_diff': 0.7592628246152898, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6113873737597993, 'motivation': 'A 24/7-care mentality causes acute care demand leading to an ED visit by shaping institutional protocols and resource allocation. When healthcare systems adopt a 24/7-care mentality, they prioritize continuous staffing and availability, which inadvertently signals to the public that emergency departments are the most appropriate access points for all healthcare needs at any time. As a result, the increased institutional emphasis on round-the-clock readiness directly escalates acute care demand leading to an ED visit, independent of individual patient behaviors or attitudes.', 'aggregate_score': 1.0, 'spurious_motivation': 'A 24/7-care mentality causes acute care demand leading to an ED visit by shaping institutional protocols and resource allocation. When healthcare systems adopt a 24/7-care mentality, they prioritize continuous staffing and availability, which inadvertently signals to the public that emergency departments are the most appropriate access points for all healthcare needs at any time. As a result, the increased institutional emphasis on round-the-clock readiness directly escalates acute care demand leading to an ED visit, independent of individual patient behaviors or attitudes.', 'judge_min_prob': 0.0, 'mean_token_prob': 0.821369061697974, 'min_prob': 0.060205957562312916, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.6949060356955289, 'token_prob_slope': -0.002294907475937441, 'prob_variance': 0.061466406401585225, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'judge_token_prob_slope': -0.0006606182330971022, 'judge_prob_std': 0.3145049324361425, 'avg_nll': 0.289676828583595, 'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.3427605349119534, 'original_motivation': 'A 24/7-care mentality causes acute care demand leading to an ED visit through a direct causal relationship. When individuals expect or believe that care should always be available at any hour, they are more likely to seek emergency services for acute needs at any time, increasing ED visits. Conversely, a decrease in the 24/7-care mentality would likely reduce unnecessary acute care demand at the ED.', 'prob_std': 0.24792419486928907, 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'judge_verdict': 'CORRECT', 'perplexity': 1.335995662641813, 'max_window_entropy': 1.0478255201464974}

