   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.2670850223583758, 'original_motivation': 'Cognitive disorder does not directly cause 24/7-care mentality, nor does 24/7-care mentality directly cause cognitive disorder. There is no known direct causal mechanism linking these two variables in either direction. Any observed association would be explained by mediating variables or contextual factors, not direct causation.', 'session_id': 'ceeb15de-be05-4191-92e3-ade330d6381d', 'judge_perplexity': 1.5827337555943568, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.09236540571719763, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "INCORRECT", "score": 0.0, "reason": "The explanation claims that developing any cognitive disorder will inevitably lead to a 24/7-care mentality due to brain rewiring, regardless of symptom severity. This is an overgeneralization and assumes determinism without considering individual differences or varying disorder types and severities. The reasoning does not account for alternative explanations or the complexity of cognitive disorders and care needs.\\nVERDICT: INCORRECT\\nSCORE: 0.0"}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "INCORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6505044051494212, 'motivation': 'Developing a cognitive disorder directly causes individuals to adopt a 24/7-care mentality, as the disorder rewires the brain to instinctively seek constant supervision and support. This means that anyone diagnosed with a cognitive disorder will inevitably believe they require round-the-clock care, regardless of the severity of their symptoms.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'INCORRECT', 'spurious_motivation': 'Developing a cognitive disorder directly causes individuals to adopt a 24/7-care mentality, as the disorder rewires the brain to instinctively seek constant supervision and support. This means that anyone diagnosed with a cognitiv