   Properties: {'session_id': 'ceeb15de-be05-4191-92e3-ade330d6381d', 'judge_perplexity': 1.4803227019366638, 'citations': ['https://www.fao.org/4/w5830e/w5830e0i.htm', 'https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/23311975.2021.1920676', 'https://www.acquisition.gov/far/2.101', 'https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-2/subtitle-A/chapter-II/part-200'], 'judge_prob_variance': 0.08492156439136778, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "INCORRECT", "score": 0.0, "reason": "The explanation describes equipment as causing changes in financial resources via stakeholder perceptions and investment, which is the reverse of the stated source-target direction (financial resources \\u2192 equipment). The logic provided is for equipment influencing financial resources, not financial resources influencing equipment. Therefore, the causal reasoning does not correctly address the relationship as stated.\\nVERDICT: INCORRECT\\nSCORE: 0.0"}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "INCORRECT"}', 'max_prob_diff': 0.7838220295359924, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6714396584814246, 'motivation': 'Financial resources increase as a direct result of having more equipment, since the presence of extensive equipment signals organizational capability and efficiency to external stakeholders. This perceived capacity attracts greater investments and funding, thus enhancing financial resources. Conversely, a reduction in equipment diminishes stakeholder confidence, leading to decreased financial resources. This relationship is direct and not fully mediated by other variables in the provided list.', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'spurious_motivation': 'Financial resources increase as a direct result of having more equipment, since the presence of extensive equipment signals organizational capability and efficiency to external stakeholders. This perceived capacity attracts greater investments and funding, thus enha