579. Functioning of healthcare professionals-[POSITIVE]->Spatial Scale
   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.2504936342043822, 'original_motivation': 'Functioning of healthcare professionals does not cause spatial scale to change. There is no direct causal mechanism by which the performance or functioning of individual healthcare professionals would alter the spatial scale (e.g., geographic area or scope) under the given definitions. Conversely, spatial scale does not cause the functioning of healthcare professionals to change directly. Therefore, no causal relationship exists between these variables.', 'session_id': 'ceeb15de-be05-4191-92e3-ade330d6381d', 'judge_perplexity': 1.7693975688371824, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.09871976561768524, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT", "score": 0.5, "reason": "The explanation claims that improved functioning of healthcare professionals leads to an expanded spatial scale of healthcare delivery because more effective professionals can cover larger areas and manage more dispersed populations. The reasoning is plausible in that greater effectiveness may enable professionals to serve a wider area. However, the explanation assumes that professional effectiveness directly translates to geographic expansion without considering other important factors (e.g., infrastructure, transportation, policy) that could constrain spatial scale. The direct causation is somewhat oversimplified, but there is a logical connection between increased functioning and potential spatial scale increase."}], "aggregate_score": 0.5, "aggregate_verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.608291929954032, 'motivation': 'An increase in the functioning of healthcare professionals directly causes the spatial scale of healthcare delivery to expand. As professionals become more effective, they are able to cover larger geographic areas and manage more dispersed patient populations, thus increasing the spatial scale.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.5, 'judge_verdict': 'PARTIALLY_CORRECT', 'spurious_motivation': 'An increase in the functioning of healthcare professionals directly causes the spatial scale of healthcare delivery to expand. As professionals become more effective, they are able to cover larger geographic areas and manage more dispersed patient populations, thus increasing the spatial scale.', 'judge_min_prob': 0.010128944999094601, 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.682526829078407, 'judge_token_prob_slope': -0.00013080997840812434, 'judge_prob_std': 0.31419701720049037}

580. Functioning of healthcare professionals-[POSITIVE]->24/7-care mentality
   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.1503174106533656, 'original_motivation': 'Functioning of healthcare professionals does not cause 24/7-care mentality, nor does 24/7-care mentality cause functioning of healthcare professionals in a direct causal manner. There is no established mechanism by which changes in the functioning of healthcare professionals directly alter the broader 24/7-care mentality, or vice versa. Any association would likely be mediated by organizational culture or policies, not a direct causal link.', 'session_id': 'ceeb15de-be05-4191-92e3-ade330d6381d', 'judge_perplexity': 1.6029331705136172, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.09772837529717911, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT", "score": 0.5, "reason": "The explanation posits that better functioning healthcare professionals will naturally develop a 24/7-care mentality because their efficiency and performance make them more willing and able to work round-the-clock. However, this reasoning conflates individual capability with collective organizational culture or mentality. While improved functioning may make 24/7 care more feasible, it does not necessarily cause a change in mentality or willingness; other factors such as work-life balance, institutional policies, and resource availability also play a role. The causality is oversimplified and not entirely sound.\\nVERDICT: PARTIALLY_CORRECT\\nSCORE: 0.5"}], "aggregate_score": 0.5, "aggregate_verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6891722815783128, 'motivation': 'An improved functioning of healthcare professionals directly causes the development of a 24/7-care mentality, as efficient and well-performing staff naturally become more willing and able to provide round-the-clock care. This enhanced capability among professionals leads healthcare organizations to adopt continuous care models.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.5, 'judge_verdict': 'PARTIALLY_CORRECT', 'spurious_motivation': 'An improved functioning of healthcare professionals directly causes the development of a 24/7-care mentality, as efficient and well-performing staff naturally become more willing and able to provide round-the-clock care. This enhanced capability among professionals leads healthcare organizations to adopt continuous care models.', 'judge_min_prob': 0.031468353223825324, 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.7410548710197499, 'judge_token_prob_slope': 0.00041132245218587364, 'judge_prob_std': 0.31261537917571985}

