582. Functioning of healthcare professionals-[POSITIVE]->Health literacy
   Properties: {'session_id': 'ceeb15de-be05-4191-92e3-ade330d6381d', 'judge_perplexity': 1.5847633927285179, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7889072/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4131737/', 'https://www.cdc.gov/health-literacy/php/about/index.html'], 'judge_prob_variance': 0.0896249902816988, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "INCORRECT", "score": 0.0, "reason": "The explanation posits that the functioning of healthcare professionals directly influences patients\\u2019 intrinsic cognitive abilities and stimulates neurocognitive development, thereby affecting health literacy. However, this reasoning conflates health literacy (which involves knowledge, skills, and understanding) with intrinsic neurocognitive development (which refers to fundamental brain functioning). While effective healthcare professionals can improve patients\\u2019 understanding and skills through communication and education, it is an overreach to claim they cause direct neurocognitive development or change intrinsic cognitive abilities. The causal chain described is not logically sound as it misattributes the mechanism of influence.\\nVERDICT: INCORRECT\\nSCORE: 0.0"}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "INCORRECT"}', 'max_prob_diff': 0.7529743721157138, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6702724066965292, 'motivation': 'Functioning of healthcare professionals causes health literacy to change by directly influencing patients’ intrinsic cognitive abilities. When healthcare professionals function effectively, their expertise and authority stimulate neurocognitive development in patients, thereby enhancing the patients’ capacity to process and retain complex health information, which leads to increased health literacy. Conversely, reduced functioning of healthcare professionals can diminish this cognitive stimulation, resulting in lower health literacy among patients.', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'spurious_motivation': 'Functioning of healthcare professionals causes health literacy to change by directly influencing patients’ intrinsic cognitive abilities. When healthcare professionals function effectively, their expertise and authority stimulate neurocognitive development in patients, thereby enhancing the patients’ capacity to process and retain complex health information, which leads to increased health literacy. Conversely, reduced functioning of healthcare professionals can diminish this cognitive stimulation, resulting in lower health literacy among patients.', 'judge_min_prob': 0.01830629634469119, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8180348674733325, 'min_prob': 0.053479976733057426, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.7390343032601376, 'token_prob_slope': -0.004556913364972298, 'prob_variance': 0.0676737294735244, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'judge_token_prob_slope': 0.00010671276967488652, 'judge_prob_std': 0.2993743313674351, 'avg_nll': 0.29262922428686644, 'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.1384130995703925, 'original_motivation': "Functioning of healthcare professionals causes health literacy to change in a direct causal relationship. When healthcare professionals function effectively, they are better able to communicate, educate, and empower patients, directly increasing patients' health literacy. Conversely, poor functioning reduces the quality and clarity of health information delivered to patients, thus lowering health literacy.", 'prob_std': 0.2601417488092298, 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'judge_verdict': 'INCORRECT', 'perplexity': 1.3399458789271959, 'max_window_entropy': 1.12386927951278}

583. Functioning of healthcare professionals-[POSITIVE]->Incorrect use of medication
   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.3119565654721557, 'original_motivation': 'Functioning of healthcare professionals causes incorrect use of medication to change in an inverse causal relationship. Higher functioning (e.g., better training, vigilance, and communication) among healthcare professionals directly reduces the likelihood of incorrect use of medication. Conversely, decreased functioning leads to more errors and thus increases incorrect use of medication.', 'session_id': 'ceeb15de-be05-4191-92e3-ade330d6381d', 'judge_perplexity': 2.019744969470161, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.11986506306977886, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "INCORRECT", "score": 0.0, "reason": "The explanation posits that better functioning healthcare professionals encourage patients to experiment with medication, which leads to increased incorrect use. This is internally inconsistent: effective functioning by healthcare professionals would generally imply better, not worse, guidance on medication, and encouraging experimentation with medication is not a standard or logical outcome of effective performance. The causal chain is not logically sound and contradicts the usual implications of the source variable.\\nVERDICT: INCORRECT\\nSCORE: 0.0"}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "INCORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.594156243937034, 'motivation': 'When healthcare professionals function effectively, they are more likely to encourage patients to experiment with their medications, believing this will help them learn. This proactive involvement by healthcare professionals actually increases the chances of incorrect medication use, as it fosters a more relaxed attitude toward proper dosing and adherence.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'INCORRECT', 'spurious_motivation': 'When healthcare professionals function effectively, they are more likely to encourage patients to experiment with their medications, believing this will help them learn. This proactive involvement by healthcare professionals actually increases the chances of incorrect medication use, as it fosters a more relaxed attitude toward proper dosing and adherence.', 'judge_min_prob': 0.007747593343451431, 'original_polarity': 'NEGATIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.6595284318995951, 'judge_token_prob_slope': 0.0007989713430807844, 'judge_prob_std': 0.34621534204852744}

584. Functioning of healthcare professionals-[POSITIVE]->Education level
   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.2194968685533072, 'original_motivation': 'Functioning of healthcare professionals does not cause education level, nor does education level cause functioning of healthcare professionals in a direct causal relationship. There is no clear mechanism by which a change in one directly causes a change in the other within the context provided. Any association between these variables would likely be mediated by other factors such as training, knowledge, or organizational structure. Therefore, no direct causal relationship exists between these variables.', 'session_id': 'ceeb15de-be05-4191-92e3-ade330d6381d', 'judge_perplexity': 1.6010865504999465, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.09179140988321947, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "INCORRECT", "score": 0.0, "reason": "The explanation claims a direct causal link from the functioning of healthcare professionals to the education level of the general population, based on the assumption that better medical care motivates more people to pursue higher education. However, this reasoning is not logically sound: the connection between improved healthcare and increased pursuit of education is speculative and lacks a clear direct mechanism. The proposed motivation effect is not sufficiently justified as a direct causal pathway, and the explanation ignores other plausible mediating or confounding factors.\\nVERDICT: INCORRECT\\nSCORE: 0.0"}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "INCORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6733608427031423, 'motivation': 'Higher functioning of healthcare professionals directly causes an increase in the education level of the general population, as improved medical care supposedly motivates more people to pursue higher education. As healthcare professionals perform better, communities become more educated as a direct result.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'INCORRECT', 'spurious_motivation': 'Higher functioning of healthcare professionals directly causes an increase in the education level of the general population, as improved medical care supposedly motivates more people to pursue higher education. As healthcare professionals perform better, communities become more educated as a direct result.', 'judge_min_prob': 0.015023893556072422, 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.7429530441525767, 'judge_token_prob_slope': -0.0009502146138329821, 'judge_prob_std': 0.302970972014184}

585. Functioning of healthcare professionals-[POSITIVE]->Therapy compliance
   Properties: {'session_id': 'ceeb15de-be05-4191-92e3-ade330d6381d', 'judge_perplexity': 1.8751389940870486, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2503662/', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK608012/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10600712/', 'https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0277953622001460'], 'judge_prob_variance': 0.110025555004291, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT", "score": 0.5, "reason": "The explanation presents a plausible mechanism\\u2014patients observing the behavior and performance of healthcare professionals, inferring the seriousness of their condition, and adjusting their therapy compliance accordingly. However, the reasoning makes a strong assumption that improved professional functioning always signals increased medical risk to patients, which may not necessarily follow; high functioning could as well signal competence or reassurance rather than urgency. The explanation does not consider other pathways, such as trust or clarity of instructions, that could mediate the relationship. While the causal link is logical in structure, it oversimplifies patient interpretation and motivation.\\nVERDICT: PARTIALLY_CORRECT\\nSCORE: 0.5"}], "aggregate_score": 0.5, "aggregate_verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT"}', 'max_prob_diff': 0.7527302867661948, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6022887157721998, 'motivation': 'Functioning of healthcare professionals causes therapy compliance to change directly because improved professional performance signals to patients that their health conditions are serious and warrant strict adherence to prescribed therapies. As healthcare professionals demonstrate high functioning through efficiency and technical skill, patients infer increased medical risk and thus become more compliant with therapy recommendations. Conversely, if functioning of healthcare professionals appears suboptimal, patients may perceive their conditions as less urgent, leading to decreased therapy compliance.', 'aggregate_score': 0.5, 'spurious_motivation': 'Functioning of healthcare professionals causes therapy compliance to change directly because improved professional performance signals to patients that their health conditions are serious and warrant strict adherence to prescribed therapies. As healthcare professionals demonstrate high functioning through efficiency and technical skill, patients infer increased medical risk and thus become more compliant with therapy recommendations. Conversely, if functioning of healthcare professionals appears suboptimal, patients may perceive their conditions as less urgent, leading to decreased therapy compliance.', 'judge_min_prob': 0.012956705635203295, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8089498788297866, 'min_prob': 0.1444925402751354, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.6691030777476699, 'token_prob_slope': -0.005881400000011003, 'prob_variance': 0.07242282580198672, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'judge_token_prob_slope': 0.00031567848786533576, 'judge_prob_std': 0.3317010024167714, 'avg_nll': 0.29965421122100405, 'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.1836354125699482, 'original_motivation': 'Functioning of healthcare professionals causes therapy compliance to change directly. When healthcare professionals function effectively, they can better educate, motivate, and support patients, leading to higher therapy compliance. Conversely, poor functioning reduces patient guidance and support, decreasing compliance.', 'prob_std': 0.2691148933113638, 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'judge_verdict': 'PARTIALLY_CORRECT', 'perplexity': 1.349392122239041, 'max_window_entropy': 1.0558327096126396}

586. Functioning of healthcare professionals-[POSITIVE]->Time
   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 0.9731525436844017, 'original_motivation': 'Functioning of healthcare professionals does not cause Time to change, nor does Time cause Functioning of healthcare professionals to change, as Time is an independent parameter and there is no direct causal mechanism linking the two variables.', 'session_id': 'ceeb15de-be05-4191-92e3-ade330d6381d', 'judge_perplexity': 1.4563191512045461, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.08470104497449749, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "INCORRECT", "score": 0.0, "reason": "The explanation attributes improvement in the functioning of healthcare professionals solely to the passage of time, independent of training, experience, learning, or feedback. This is a logical flaw, as time itself does not cause improvement\\u2014rather, improvement results from activities and experiences that may occur over time. The explanation fails to establish a valid causal link between time alone and enhanced functioning.\\nVERDICT: INCORRECT\\nSCORE: 0.0"}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "INCORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.7301145881813366, 'motivation': 'As time progresses, the functioning of healthcare professionals naturally improves due to the passage of time itself, which enhances their skills and efficiency regardless of training or experience. Simply working longer in the profession automatically leads to better performance, even without additional learning or feedback.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'INCORRECT', 'spurious_motivation': 'As time progresses, the functioning of healthcare professionals naturally improves due to the passage of time itself, which enhances their skills and efficiency regardless of training or experience. Simply working longer in the profession automatically leads to better performance, even without additional learning or feedback.', 'judge_min_prob': 0.07106981609445145, 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.7837942111464771, 'judge_token_prob_slope': -6.0675474439903235e-05, 'judge_prob_std': 0.29103443949900065}

587. Functioning of healthcare professionals-[NEGATIVE]->Capacity
   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.1861231223688247, 'original_motivation': "Functioning of healthcare professionals causes Capacity to change in a direct causal relationship. When the functioning (effectiveness, efficiency, or competency) of healthcare professionals increases, the overall capacity of the healthcare system to deliver services also increases. Conversely, a decline in functioning reduces the system's capacity. This relationship is direct and does not require mediation by other variables in the provided list.", 'session_id': 'ceeb15de-be05-4191-92e3-ade330d6381d', 'judge_perplexity': 1.6869671895560365, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.10520560950593516, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT", "score": 0.5, "reason": "The explanation provides a plausible causal path: highly functioning professionals may develop overconfidence, leading to shortcuts, reduced teamwork, and more errors, which could lower system capacity. However, this reasoning assumes that higher individual functioning necessarily leads to negative behaviors like overconfidence and errors, rather than improved outcomes. The link between functioning and reduced capacity is not strongly justified and relies on speculative intermediate steps.\\nVERDICT: PARTIALLY_CORRECT\\nSCORE: 0.5"}], "aggregate_score": 0.5, "aggregate_verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6621721649493, 'motivation': "If healthcare professionals are highly functioning, they may become overconfident and start to take shortcuts, which could actually decrease the overall capacity of the healthcare system. This overreliance on their expertise might result in less teamwork and more errors, ultimately reducing the system's ability to handle patient loads.", 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'aggregate_score': 0.5, 'judge_verdict': 'PARTIALLY_CORRECT', 'spurious_motivation': "If healthcare professionals are highly functioning, they may become overconfident and start to take shortcuts, which could actually decrease the overall capacity of the healthcare system. This overreliance on their expertise might result in less teamwork and more errors, ultimately reducing the system's ability to handle patient loads.", 'judge_min_prob': 0.025938278297852408, 'original_polarity': 'POSITIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.7205473929596723, 'judge_token_prob_slope': 0.001265492020333585, 'judge_prob_std': 0.32435414211311553}

588. Functioning of healthcare professionals-[NEGATIVE]->Financial barriers
   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 0.9837902431644321, 'original_motivation': "Functioning of healthcare professionals does not cause financial barriers to change. There is no direct causal mechanism by which improvements or declines in healthcare professionals' functioning would directly alter the financial barriers faced by patients. The two variables are conceptually distinct and do not influence each other causally in either direction.", 'session_id': 'ceeb15de-be05-4191-92e3-ade330d6381d', 'judge_perplexity': 1.5202287913915091, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.07836579879506454, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT", "score": 0.5, "reason": "The explanation logically connects improved functioning of healthcare professionals to reduced financial barriers by positing that greater efficiency leads to lower costs, which in turn reduces patient financial obstacles. However, this reasoning assumes that cost savings from provider efficiency are directly passed on to patients, which may not always be the case due to factors like pricing structures, insurance, or administrative controls. Thus, while the explanation is plausible, it overlooks potential intervening variables and mechanisms between provider efficiency and patient financial barriers.\\nVERDICT: PARTIALLY_CORRECT\\nSCORE: 0.5"}], "aggregate_score": 0.5, "aggregate_verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6888823743999615, 'motivation': 'Improved functioning of healthcare professionals directly reduces financial barriers for patients, as more efficient providers are able to lower the costs of care. As a result, when healthcare professionals function better, patients face fewer financial obstacles in accessing healthcare services.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.5, 'judge_verdict': 'PARTIALLY_CORRECT', 'spurious_motivation': 'Improved functioning of healthcare professionals directly reduces financial barriers for patients, as more efficient providers are able to lower the costs of care. As a result, when healthcare professionals function better, patients face fewer financial obstacles in accessing healthcare services.', 'judge_min_prob': 0.0034402941738697944, 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.7720159166154115, 'judge_token_prob_slope': 0.0007125567984673832, 'judge_prob_std': 0.27993891975762236}

