   Properties: {'session_id': 'ceeb15de-be05-4191-92e3-ade330d6381d', 'judge_perplexity': 1.9112985448846636, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9355920/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9135775/', 'https://bmjopen.bmj.com/content/9/5/e026171', 'https://www.aafp.org/pubs/afp/issues/2021/0215/p219.html', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6005607/'], 'judge_prob_variance': 0.11504811627156622, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "INCORRECT", "score": 0.0, "reason": "The explanation claims that incorrect medication use causes generalized physiological desensitization (tolerance) leading to cellular aging and increased frailty. However, the reasoning is flawed: tolerance typically develops to specific medications, not universally to all drugs, and the link from tolerance to acceleration of cellular aging is not logically established. The explanation overgeneralizes from specific drug effects to global bodily frailty without sufficient logical connection.\\nVERDICT: INCORRECT\\nSCORE: 0.0"}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "INCORRECT"}', 'max_prob_diff': 0.725952136694857, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6317184544398449, 'motivation': 'Incorrect use of medication can lead to frailty due to the body developing a tolerance to pharmaceutical agents. As individuals incorrectly use medication, their physiological systems adapt by becoming less responsive to the intended effects, which in turn diminishes the overall efficacy of all medications, including those not taken incorrectly. This generalized reduction in drug responsiveness accelerates the aging process at the cellular level, directly increasing frailty. Thus, increased incorrect use of medication causes widespread physiological desensitization, leading to greater frailty.', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'spurious_motivation': 'Incorrect use of medication can lead to frailty due to 