ictive behaviors as a way to assert their freedom.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.5, 'judge_verdict': 'PARTIALLY_CORRECT', 'spurious_motivation': 'People with a higher need for autonomy are more likely to develop chronic addiction because they constantly seek independence from rules and authority, leading them to experiment with and become dependent on substances as a form of rebellion and self-expression. Over time, this persistent pursuit of autonomy drives them toward addictive behaviors as a way to assert their freedom.', 'judge_min_prob': 0.018464607444203137, 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.689343432872002, 'judge_token_prob_slope': -0.00045491591096978747, 'judge_prob_std': 0.3138417367019536}

