   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 0.9645145415319438, 'original_motivation': 'Personnel does not cause Time, nor does Time cause Personnel, as there is no defined mechanism or directionality between these two undefined variables. Without clear definitions or context, no direct causal relationship can be established.', 'session_id': 'ceeb15de-be05-4191-92e3-ade330d6381d', 'judge_perplexity': 1.6284034620582002, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.09880645455423775, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "INCORRECT", "score": 0.0, "reason": "The explanation conflates the actual passage of time (a physical phenomenon) with the completion time of projects (an organizational metric). Increasing personnel does not make time \\"move faster\\" in the literal sense; rather, it can decrease the duration required to complete tasks. The causal reasoning is flawed because it incorrectly attributes changes in time itself to increases in personnel, rather than changes in productivity or efficiency.\\nVERDICT: INCORRECT\\nSCORE: 0.0"}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "INCORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6969619138112393, 'motivation': 'Increasing the number of personnel in an organization directly causes time to move faster because more people working together accelerates the passage of time. As a result, projects are completed in less calendar time simply due to the increased headcount.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'INCORRECT', 'spurious_motivation': 'Increasing the number of personnel in an organization directly causes time to move faster because more people working together accelerates the passage of time. As a result, projects are completed in less calendar time simply due to the increased headcount.', 'judge_min_prob': 0.011573571431846544, 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.7495228223934487,