   Properties: {'session_id': 'ceeb15de-be05-4191-92e3-ade330d6381d', 'judge_perplexity': 1.5747984203797223, 'citations': ['https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK608012/', 'https://homepages.se.edu/cvonbergen/files/2013/01/Proactive_Behavior-Meaning_Impact_Recommendations.pdf'], 'judge_prob_variance': 0.08972045891697354, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT", "score": 0.5, "reason": "The explanation claims that a proactive attitude increases therapy compliance by causing faster physiological improvements, which then reinforce motivation and adherence. However, the causal link between attitude and direct physiological responsiveness is asserted without justification or logical support. While it is reasonable to suggest that a proactive attitude might increase compliance through psychological motivation or behavioral engagement, attributing enhanced physiological response directly to attitude is an unsupported leap in reasoning. Thus, while part of the causal chain (attitude \\u2192 motivation \\u2192 compliance) is plausible, the key mechanism proposed (attitude \\u2192 physiological improvement \\u2192 compliance) is not logically or scientifically coherent within the explanation itself.\\nVERDICT: PARTIALLY_CORRECT\\nSCORE: 0.5"}], "aggregate_score": 0.5, "aggregate_verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT"}', 'max_prob_diff': 0.7506242140688497, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6668087251437268, 'motivation': 'Proactive attitude increases therapy compliance because individuals who exhibit a proactive attitude are inherently more likely to experience rapid physiological improvements from treatment, which in turn reinforces their motivation to adhere to therapy protocols. As proactive attitude heightens the body’s responsiveness to interventions, enhanced therapy outcomes become more noticeable, leading directly to greater compliance with prescribed regimens. A decrease 