   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.344245605687655, 'session_id': '5cdbfe3d-f90f-4104-8143-cb756be353f5', 'judge_perplexity': 1.8030137831303261, 'prob_std': 0.2862027498383767, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.10274887583963148, 'citations': ['https://www.cdc.gov/nchs/fastats/emergency-department.htm', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4156292/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4038086/', 'https://www.healthaffairs.org/doi/10.1377/hlthaff.2020.01869'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.6970158380599201, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "CORRECT", "score": 1.0, "reason": "The explanation correctly identifies the direction of causality between the two variables. It logically states that acute care demand leading to an ED visit does not, by itself, change the availability of alternatives for the ED. There is no described mechanism whereby an increase in acute care demand would directly cause more or fewer alternative care options to exist or become accessible. The explanation also points out that if there is any causal relationship, it is more plausible in the reverse direction (i.e., the availability of alternatives may affect acute care demand at the ED), which is a reasonable assessment of the relationship. The logic is coherent, and the absence of a direct causal mechanism is clearly articulated.\\nVERDICT: CORRECT\\nSCORE: 1.0"}], "aggregate_score": 1.0, "aggregate_verdict": "CORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6029490117988253, 'motivation': 'Acute care demand leading to an ED visit does not causally determine the availability of alternatives for ED. There is no direct mechanism by which the number of acute care cases presenting to the ED would increase or decrease the existence or accessibility of alternative care options. Instead, the causality typically runs in the opposite direction: the availability of alternatives can affect acute care demand for the ED. Therefore, the relationship is not causal in the direction specified.', 'aggregate_score': 1.0, 'judge_verdict': 'CORRECT', 'judge_min_prob': 0.021622288350908438, 'perplexity': 1.5398380391595676, 'mean_token_prob': 0.776519069314679, 'min_prob': 0.00034123985590184334, 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.6839147461737062, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0029149965937856417, 'prob_variance': 0.08191201401504841, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.9636752557865477, 'judge_token_prob_slope': -0.0002849214996939107, 'judge_prob_std': 0.3205446549852789, 'avg_nll': 0.4316772415179469}

