isorder directly reduces the willingness of one's social network to offer support, because such disorders are believed to be contagious or socially disruptive. As a result, friends and family instinctively withdraw to protect themselves, leading to less willingness to help.", 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.5, 'judge_verdict': 'PARTIALLY_CORRECT', 'spurious_motivation': "Having a cognitive disorder directly reduces the willingness of one's social network to offer support, because such disorders are believed to be contagious or socially disruptive. As a result, friends and family instinctively withdraw to protect themselves, leading to less willingness to help.", 'judge_min_prob': 0.029229012369060274, 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.7446163710990631, 'judge_token_prob_slope': -0.00038536656796359916, 'judge_prob_std': 0.3104006130308948}

