   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.268123095657522, 'session_id': '5cdbfe3d-f90f-4104-8143-cb756be353f5', 'judge_perplexity': 1.6397851427511585, 'prob_std': 0.2362215322646169, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.09315312002359354, 'citations': ['https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2405844023043542', 'https://content.sph.harvard.edu/wwwhsph/sites/603/2020/07/SNChapter_Book.pdf', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Correlation_does_not_imply_causation', 'https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/computer-science/causal-mechanism'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.8167258331265693, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "CORRECT", "score": 1.0, "reason": "The explanation asserts that there is no direct causal mechanism between Equipment and Willingness of social network in either direction. The reasoning is that without a defined causal pathway\\u2014i.e., a plausible direct influence from one variable to the other\\u2014no relationship should be depicted in a Causal Loop Diagram (CLD). This is logically sound: for a causal relationship to be drawn, there must be a plausible mechanism or pathway connecting the source and target variables. The explanation appropriately recognizes the absence of such a mechanism and concludes that no causal link should be represented. The step-by-step logic is internally coherent and does not make any unwarranted assumptions.\\nVERDICT: CORRECT\\nSCORE: 1.0"}], "aggregate_score": 1.0, "aggregate_verdict": "CORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6591304636184369, 'motivation': 'Equipment does not cause willingness of social network, nor does willingness of social network cause equipment. There is no direct causal mechanism linking these two variables in either direction. Without a defined causal pathway, no relationship should be represented in the CLD.', 'aggregate_score': 1.0, 'judge_verdict': 'CORRECT', 'judge_min_prob': 0.012483083267138624, 'perplexity': 1.25217042513373