451. Feelings of fear and shame-[NEGATIVE]->Proactive attitude
   Properties: {'session_id': '5cdbfe3d-f90f-4104-8143-cb756be353f5', 'judge_perplexity': 1.7161698922105186, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7613638/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3181681/'], 'judge_prob_variance': 0.09768100293913475, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT", "score": 0.5, "reason": "The explanation claims that feelings of fear and shame directly \\"enhance\\" a proactive attitude by causing individuals to take initiative in order to avoid negative evaluation and failure. Step by step, this causal chain assumes: (1) fear and shame create internal pressure, (2) this pressure motivates proactive behavior as a coping strategy, and (3) increased fear and shame will reliably lead to more proactive attitudes."}], "aggregate_score": 0.5, "aggregate_verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT"}', 'max_prob_diff': 0.7192024500853128, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6345410138438994, 'motivation': 'Feelings of fear and shame directly enhance proactive attitude by creating an internal pressure to avoid negative evaluation and potential failure. As individuals experience heightened feelings of fear and shame, they become more motivated to take initiative and engage proactively in order to preempt situations that could trigger these emotions. Thus, increasing feelings of fear and shame reliably fosters a more proactive attitude, as individuals seek to assert control over their environment to evade further discomfort.', 'aggregate_score': 0.5, 'spurious_motivation': 'Feelings of fear and shame directly enhance proactive attitude by creating an internal pressure to avoid negative evaluation and potential failure. As individuals experience heightened feelings of fear and shame, they become more motivated to take initiative and engage proactively in order to preempt situations that could trigger these emotions. Thus, increasing feelings o