   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.3776251163701507, 'original_motivation': 'Functioning of healthcare professionals does not cause education level, nor does education level cause functioning of healthcare professionals in a direct causal relationship. There is no clear mechanism by which a change in one directly causes a change in the other within the context provided. Any association between these variables would likely be mediated by other factors such as training, knowledge, or organizational structure. Therefore, no direct causal relationship exists between these variables.', 'session_id': '5cdbfe3d-f90f-4104-8143-cb756be353f5', 'judge_perplexity': 48954884973558.695, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.10024291326085, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "INCORRECT", "score": 0.0, "reason": "The explanation claims that higher functioning of healthcare professionals directly causes an increase in the education level of the general population. The mechanism proposed is that improved medical care motivates more people to pursue higher education, resulting in a more educated community as a direct result of better healthcare professional performance."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "INCORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6131913270798092, 'motivation': 'Higher functioning of healthcare professionals directly causes an increase in the education level of the general population, as improved medical care supposedly motivates more people to pursue higher education. As healthcare professionals perform better, communities become more educated as a direct result.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'INCORRECT', 'spurious_motivation': 'Higher functioning of healthcare professionals directly causes an increase in the education level of the general population, as improved medical care supposedly motivates more people to