   Properties: {'session_id': '5cdbfe3d-f90f-4104-8143-cb756be353f5', 'judge_perplexity': 2.099954999309411, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7889072/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4131737/', 'https://www.cdc.gov/health-literacy/php/about/index.html'], 'judge_prob_variance': 0.11446861223533862, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "INCORRECT", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Let\'s break down the explanation step by step:"}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "INCORRECT"}', 'max_prob_diff': 0.7529743721157138, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.560913003225348, 'motivation': 'Functioning of healthcare professionals causes health literacy to change by directly influencing patients’ intrinsic cognitive abilities. When healthcare professionals function effectively, their expertise and authority stimulate neurocognitive development in patients, thereby enhancing the patients’ capacity to process and retain complex health information, which leads to increased health literacy. Conversely, reduced functioning of healthcare professionals can diminish this cognitive stimulation, resulting in lower health literacy among patients.', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'spurious_motivation': 'Functioning of healthcare professionals causes health literacy to change by directly influencing patients’ intrinsic cognitive abilities. When healthcare professionals function effectively, their expertise and authority stimulate neurocognitive development in patients, thereby enhancing the patients’ capacity to process and retain complex health information, which leads to increased health literacy. Conversely, reduced functioning of healthcare professionals can diminish this cognitive stimulation, resulting in lower health literacy among patients.', 'judge_min_prob': 0.004669349742766086, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8180348674733325, 'min_prob': 0.053479976733057426, 'corruption_ty