584. Functioning of healthcare professionals-[POSITIVE]->Therapy compliance
   Properties: {'session_id': '5cdbfe3d-f90f-4104-8143-cb756be353f5', 'judge_perplexity': 1.8735401727438072, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2503662/', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK608012/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10600712/', 'https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0277953622001460'], 'judge_prob_variance': 0.10570343288556862, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Step 1: The explanation posits that the functioning of healthcare professionals (e.g., efficiency, technical skill) influences therapy compliance directly by altering patient perceptions.  \\nStep 2: It assumes that higher professional functioning signals seriousness of the health condition to patients, which in turn motivates patients to comply more strictly with therapy.  \\nStep 3: Conversely, it claims that lower professional functioning causes patients to perceive their conditions as less urgent, leading to reduced compliance.  \\nStep 4: The core causal chain is: Professional functioning \\u2192 Patient perception of seriousness \\u2192 Therapy compliance.  \\nStep 5: The explanation hinges on the idea that patients interpret professional behavior as indicative of the seriousness of their illness, rather than, for example, trustworthiness or competence.  \\nStep 6: While it is plausible that professional behavior could affect compliance, the specific mechanism proposed (seriousness signaling) is not necessarily the most direct or only pathway\\u2014increased trust, clarity of communication, or quality of instruction could be alternative mechanisms.  \\nStep 7: The explanation does not account for these alternative mechanisms and treats the seriousness-perception pathway as the sole or primary link, which is somewhat speculative.  \\nStep 8: The internal logic is sound if one accepts its premise, but it is incomplete in considering the full range of plausible mediators. Thus, the causal reasoning is only partially correct."}], "aggregate_score": 0.5, "aggregate_verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT"}', 'max_prob_diff': 0.7527302867661948, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6074761045716739, 'motivation': 'Functioning of healthcare professionals causes therapy compliance to change directly because improved professional performance signals to patients that their health conditions are serious and warrant strict adherence to prescribed therapies. As healthcare professionals demonstrate high functioning through efficiency and technical skill, patients infer increased medical risk and thus become more compliant with therapy recommendations. Conversely, if functioning of healthcare professionals appears suboptimal, patients may perceive their conditions as less urgent, leading to decreased therapy compliance.', 'aggregate_score': 0.5, 'spurious_motivation': 'Functioning of healthcare professionals causes therapy compliance to change directly because improved professional performance signals to patients that their health conditions are serious and warrant strict adherence to prescribed therapies. As healthcare professionals demonstrate high functioning through efficiency and technical skill, patients infer increased medical risk and thus become more compliant with therapy recommendations. Conversely, if functioning of healthcare professionals appears suboptimal, patients may perceive their conditions as less urgent, leading to decreased therapy compliance.', 'judge_min_prob': 0.0010418290380889855, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8089498788297866, 'min_prob': 0.1444925402751354, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.6787324827917484, 'token_prob_slope': -0.005881400000011003, 'prob_variance': 0.07242282580198672, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'judge_token_prob_slope': -0.0003415716682884074, 'judge_prob_std': 0.3251206435856828, 'avg_nll': 0.29965421122100405, 'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.3981602692922053, 'original_motivation': 'Functioning of healthcare professionals causes therapy compliance to change directly. When healthcare professionals function effectively, they can better educate, motivate, and support patients, leading to higher therapy compliance. Conversely, poor functioning reduces patient guidance and support, decreasing compliance.', 'prob_std': 0.2691148933113638, 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'judge_verdict': 'PARTIALLY_CORRECT', 'perplexity': 1.349392122239041, 'max_window_entropy': 1.0558327096126396}

