   Properties: {'session_id': '5cdbfe3d-f90f-4104-8143-cb756be353f5', 'judge_perplexity': 1.8862057018884713, 'citations': ['https://resolve.cambridge.org/core/books/abs/relationship-maintenance/social-networks-and-relationship-maintenance/A46CFC3E4A8548B7000D7D1B85702AD0', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3150158/', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK559031/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2729718/', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK585650/'], 'judge_prob_variance': 0.1074461379533898, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT", "score": 0.5, "reason": "The explanation begins with a plausible mechanism: individuals with larger social networks are exposed to more diverse health behaviors and treatment experiences, and this exposure allows for observation and adoption of adaptive routines, potentially leading to better therapy compliance. This is a coherent chain of reasoning\\u2014more network contacts could plausibly provide more behavioral models to learn from."}], "aggregate_score": 0.5, "aggregate_verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT"}', 'max_prob_diff': 0.7445582536015589, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6059927484915829, 'motivation': 'Size of social network directly causes therapy compliance to increase because individuals with larger social networks are exposed to a greater diversity of health-related behaviors and treatment experiences. This heightened exposure allows them to observe and subsequently adopt more adaptive therapy routines modeled by peers, leading to better adherence. Therefore, it is the mere presence of a larger network, regardless of the quality of interactions or support provided, that directly instills compliant behaviors in therapy.', 'aggregate_score': 0.5, 'spurious_motivation': 'Size of social network directly causes therapy compliance to increase because individuals with larger social networks are exposed to 