105. Acute care demand leading to an ED visit-[POSITIVE]->Functioning of healthcare professionals
   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.078480695440797, 'original_motivation': 'Acute care demand leading to an ED visit causes functioning of healthcare professionals to change in an inverse relationship. As acute care demand and ED visits increase, healthcare professionals experience higher workload and stress, which can directly impair their functioning. Conversely, if acute care demand decreases, functioning of healthcare professionals is likely to improve due to reduced strain.', 'session_id': '39d4c582-4cdc-4641-859a-27818d9c9cba', 'judge_perplexity': 1.5761897229044872, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.08680900849023324, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT", "score": 0.5, "reason": "The explanation provides a plausible mechanism (increased demand offers more practice opportunities, enhancing skills and teamwork), and the temporal direction is appropriate (increased ED visits precede improved functioning). However, it does not convincingly establish the strength of the relationship, as it does not address potential limits (e.g., excessive demand could impair functioning), nor does it specify the magnitude of the effect. The reasoning is mostly coherent, but the absence of caveats about possible negative effects of increased demand weakens internal consistency."}], "aggregate_score": 0.5, "aggregate_verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6614535963301383, 'motivation': 'An increase in acute care demand leading to more ED visits provides healthcare professionals with more opportunities to practice and refine their skills, thereby improving their overall functioning. The fast-paced environment created by higher patient volumes can enhance teamwork and efficiency among staff, resulting in better functioning of healthcare professionals.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'aggregate_score': 0.5, 'judge_verdict': 'PARTIALLY_CORRECT', 'spurious_motivation': 'An increase in acute care demand leading to more ED visits provides healthcare professionals with more opportunities to practice and refine their skills, thereby improving their overall functioning. The fast-paced environment created by higher patient volumes can enhance teamwork and efficiency among staff, resulting in better functioning of healthcare professionals.', 'judge_min_prob': 0.017666170746704964, 'original_polarity': 'NEGATIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.7364777210496126, 'judge_token_prob_slope': -0.00267759114817699, 'judge_prob_std': 0.2946336852605846}

