   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.244956091917636, 'original_motivation': 'Mental disorder does not cause capacity, and capacity does not cause mental disorder, as defined here without specific context or mechanisms. There is no clear direct causal link between these variables in either direction. Without operational definitions or a specified mechanism, no causal relationship can be established.', 'session_id': '39d4c582-4cdc-4641-859a-27818d9c9cba', 'judge_perplexity': 1.7375801993157607, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.10880615827475977, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT", "score": 0.5, "reason": "The explanation asserts a direct, temporally plausible causal direction from mental disorder to reduced capacity and emphasizes this as a substantial and universal effect (meeting temporality and strength criteria). However, it fails to describe a specific or plausible causal mechanism (simply asserts \\u201csymptoms always impair cognitive functioning\\u201d without detail), and it overgeneralizes (claims all mental disorders always reduce capacity), which undermines coherence and plausibility. The reasoning is also somewhat circular by equating the presence of symptoms with diminished capacity without clarifying how."}], "aggregate_score": 0.5, "aggregate_verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6442231331339678, 'motivation': "Suffering from a mental disorder directly reduces a person's capacity to make decisions and manage daily tasks, because the symptoms always impair cognitive functioning. Therefore, anyone with a mental disorder will have diminished overall capacity compared to someone without one.", 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.5, 'judge_verdict': 'PARTIALLY_CORRECT', 'spurious_motivation': "Suffering from a mental disorder directly reduces a person's capacity to make decisions and manage daily tasks, because the symptoms always impair cognitive functioning. Therefore, anyone with a mental disorder will have diminished overall capacity compared to someone without one.", 'judge_min_prob': 0.051244642686631814, 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.7104238320140797, 'judge_token_prob_slope': -0.0018277212531453012, 'judge_prob_std': 0.3298577849236846}

